### Working hypothesis test outcomes

| WH | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| WH1 | Evidenced (structural) | Confirmed: TPA default reporting is benefit-category, not condition-cohort. ICD-10 codes are captured in hospital claims but not delivered as cohort views in standard contracts. Five structural root causes identified across PP 2.1 and 2.4. |
| WH4 | Partially evidenced | Confirmed structurally: TPA fee models reward claim throughput, not avoided claims. No Indonesian TPA operates under an outcomes-linked fee contract. Root causes identified (regulatory definition, annual contract cycle, no benchmark). However, HealthMetrics Indonesia's 2025 launch suggests early movement toward analytics-differentiated TPA positioning — weakening the absolute version of WH4, though not resolving it. |



