| WH | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| WH2 | Partially evidenced | Confirmed structurally for insurer-bundled MCU panels: standard panels default to fasting glucose + total cholesterol; HbA1c appears only in premium/add-on tiers. Not fully evidenced because no insurer has published a complete group MCU panel specification; ASSUMED-2 remains open. Cross-reference Stage 4 for MCU provider side. |
| WH3 | Not tested at insurer stage | Productivity loss is a Stage 6 cost-of-illness question. Insurer side: no Indonesian insurer currently underwrites or quantifies productivity loss in its group health pricing or reporting. [ASSUMED-7] tags the trend-savings estimate. |
| WH4 | Evidenced (structural) | Fully confirmed: Indonesia 138% loss ratio 2023 → repricing 2024, not CDM investment. Annual contract cycle incompatible with 3–5 year CDM ROI payback. POJK 36/2025 regulatory response is cost-containment, not prevention incentive. No Indonesian insurer operates a CDM co-investment program in its group health book. |
| WH5 | Evidenced (insurer side) | HbA1c add-on cost: Rp 160,000 / USD 10.30 per employee vs. Rp 100–400 million per complication hospitalization. Incremental MCU cost is small. But procurement decisions for MCU riders sit with HR/admin teams benchmarking price, not against avoided claims — confirmed. |

